          <ul class="how" role="list">
            <li><b>Cut</b> a line, as a landslide or an earthquake might, and watch the flow find another way.</li>
            <li><b>I₀</b>: at about 3 the mold's network costs as much as the paper's, and almost nothing can cut it off.</li>
            <li><b>Start over</b> and it spreads from Tokyo again. Each run finds its own network.</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="pane__note">
            The map is stylized. Cities sit at rounded positions, the coast is a sketch, and the rail network is straight links along the main lines, so read the comparison as an illustration, not a measurement.
